  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q4-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "For what values of $k$ would the graph of $x^2+6x+y^2+k=0$ not exist?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k>9$",
      "worked": "Completing the square:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+6x+9-9+y^2+k&=0\\\\(x+3)^2+y^2&=9-k\\end{align*}$$\nThe left-hand side is non-negative, so there are no real points when\n$$\\begin{align*}9-k&<0\\\\k&>9.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 34
  },
